{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "units": [
    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianMarginalPoincare.actual_gaussian_marginal_centered_poincare",
      "title": "Poincare for the actual Gaussian Gibbs marginal",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
          "label": "PBPS2609.06905v1 Eq2.13 and AppendixD.2 D6/D10 feeding C3; original C2, two Hessian bounds,0<alpha<=beta and capped positive eta remain.",
          "scope": "Actual normalized Gibbs/Gaussian marginal nu has one genuine dense closable compact-gradient G and closed closure, selected before every centered z in its domain; alpha/(1+alpha eta)||z||²<=||Gbar z||². Original C2/two global Hessian bounds,0<alpha<=beta,eta>0,beta eta<=1 retained; finite Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicitly extends source Euclidean setting. Actual56 SAME T/K image and internally derived stationarity/centering consume this for C3 and exactrho contraction. Full weakH1/macro-range/B13/Gamma/dynamics/main/errors/cost/composition remain open."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.GaussianMarginalPoincare"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite real Hilbert/Borel E with canonical volume, including rank0 explicit source extension.",
        "V C2,0<α≤β and both global Hessian bounds;η>0 andβη≤1. The cap is retained although standalone PI needs less; actual sharp source consumer uses it.",
        "Uniform genuine G before all centered z in its closed domain. Centering restricts the PI conclusion; no supplied operator/domain/law/PI or extra moment certificate.",
        "Ḡ is exactly the closed smooth-compact gradient. Separately defined source weakH1 and onto macro range equivalences are not inferred."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, α‖a‖²≤D²V(x)[a,a]≤β‖a‖² for every x,a, η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Then ν is a probability. There exists one densely defined closable real linear gradient G:L²(ν)⇀L²(ν;E), whose graph consists exactly of AE classes (φ,∇φ) for smooth compactly supported φ, and whose closure has closed graph. For every z in domḠ with ∫z dν=0, [α/(1+αη)]‖z‖²≤‖Ḡz‖². The same G is chosen before every such z. No caller normalization, curvature, Poincare, law, domain, convergence or extra moment certificate is assumed. This is the genuine compact-gradient closure formulation of the source marginal PI; equivalence with a separately defined weighted H1 remains open.",
      "formula": "\\nu=\\operatorname{Law}(X+\\sqrt\\eta Z),\\quad m_\\eta=\\frac{\\alpha}{1+\\alpha\\eta};\\qquad\\forall z\\in\\operatorname{dom}\\overline G,\\ \\int z\\,d\\nu=0\\Rightarrow m_\\eta\\|z\\|_{L^2(\\nu)}^2\\le\\|\\overline Gz\\|_{L^2(\\nu;E)}^2.",
      "boundary": "Actual normalized Gibbs/Gaussian marginal nu has one genuine dense closable compact-gradient G and closed closure, selected before every centered z in its domain; alpha/(1+alpha eta)||z||²<=||Gbar z||². Original C2/two global Hessian bounds,0<alpha<=beta,eta>0,beta eta<=1 retained; finite Hilbert/Borel/rank0 explicitly extends source Euclidean setting. Actual56 SAME T/K image and internally derived stationarity/centering consume this for C3 and exactrho contraction. Full weakH1/macro-range/B13/Gamma/dynamics/main/errors/cost/composition remain open.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Derive the actual marginal law and its potential",
          "text": "Original lower curvature and C2 yield positive finite ZV and probability μ. The existing smoothed Gibbs producer gives Aη(y)=cη∫exp(−V(x)−‖y−x‖²/(2η))dx, positive C2 Vη=−logAη, ∫Aη=ZV and the exact actual add-noise law ν=volume.tilted(−Vη). The normalized negative-log density Uη differs from Vη by logZV; no normalizer or law equality is supplied.",
          "formula": "\\nu=\\mathrm{vol}.\\mathrm{tilted}(-V_\\eta),\\quad A_\\eta=e^{-V_\\eta}>0,\\quad\\int A_\\eta=Z_V>0,\\quad U_\\eta=V_\\eta+\\log Z_V.",
          "lean": "SmoothedGibbsPotential.smoothed_gibbs_potential; htilt; hIA; hIntA; hA; hC2; hshift; Measure.map_map"
        },
        {
          "title": "Produce the true conditional covariance bound",
          "text": "The actual Gaussian derivative producer supplies probability and vectorL2 moments of R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)). Derive R_y=volume.tilted(−W_y) with W_y(x)=V(x)+‖x−y‖²/(2η). Its genuine Hessian lies between α+η⁻¹ and β+η⁻¹. Strong convexity gives exp-L1 and a positive partition internally. Existing original-domain covariance upper applies to the actual posterior and its produced moments; no covariance or moment certificate is a theorem premise.",
          "formula": "W_y(x)=V(x)+\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^2}{2\\eta},\\quad(\\alpha+\\eta^{-1})I\\preceq D^2W_y\\preceq(\\beta+\\eta^{-1})I,\\quad\\operatorname{Var}_{R_y}\\langle a,X\\rangle\\le\\frac{\\|a\\|^2}{\\alpha+\\eta^{-1}}.",
          "lean": "GaussianConvolutionRegularity.gaussian_convolution_derivatives; hRm; hcov; hWdd; hb; hiW; hRW; GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper"
        },
        {
          "title": "Obtain both exact marginal curvature constants",
          "text": "The actual normalized Hessian identity and additive partition shift imply D²Vη(y)[a,a]=‖a‖²/η−CovR_y(a,a)/η². The produced covariance upper gives mη=α/(1+αη). Reuse the already verified generic SmoothedHessianUpper producer for Mη=β/(1+βη); it retains the true Cramer-Rao/posterior inputs and is not replaced by a coarse certificate. α≤β gives mη≤Mη.",
          "formula": "D^2V_\\eta(y)[a,a]=\\frac{\\|a\\|^2}{\\eta}-\\frac{\\operatorname{Cov}_{R_y}(a,a)}{\\eta^2},\\quad0<m_\\eta=\\frac\\alpha{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\le M_\\eta=\\frac\\beta{1+\\beta\\eta},\\quad m_\\eta I\\preceq D^2V_\\eta\\preceq M_\\eta I.",
          "lean": "hDD; he; hd; hlower; SmoothedHessianUpper.smoothed_hessian_upper; hupper; hm; hmM"
        },
        {
          "title": "Apply Poincare on the genuine closed gradient domain",
          "text": "The actual Gaussian marginal gradient producer constructs the dense smooth-compact graph G, closability and its closed closure. The actual potential has exp-L1 and a positive partition from step1. The existing centered-domain Poincare producer applies to this exact G under both derived curvature bounds. Thus one G works for every centered member of its genuine closed domain. This is a scoped closure result; the original source weakH1 identification remains a separate obligation.",
          "formula": "\\operatorname{graph}G=\\{([\\varphi],[\\nabla\\varphi]):\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty\\},\\quad\\overline{\\operatorname{dom}G}=L^2(\\nu),\\quad\\int z\\,d\\nu=0\\Rightarrow m_\\eta\\|z\\|^2\\le\\|\\overline Gz\\|^2.",
          "lean": "GaussianMarginalGradient.gaussian_marginal_gradient_closable; hI; hZη; CenteredDomainPoincare.gibbs_centered_domain_poincare; hPI"
        },
        {
          "title": "Derive domain agreement and centeredness for the real mean",
          "text": "The real consumer obtains G56,T56,K56 from the actual rough mean-gradient theorem. The two exact compact graph iff statements over the same ν imply G56=G57 and hence equality of their closures; the genuine pair (T56u,K56u) transfers internally. Actual55 constructs the literal reflected Markov S with a conditional joint Λ and both marginals ν. Using actual56 AE source means and actual disintegration gives ∫T56u dν=∫u dν for every L2 input. Thus centered u gives centered T56u; no output-centering/domain certificate is supplied.",
          "formula": "G_{56}=G_{57},\\quad(Tu,Ku)\\in\\operatorname{graph}\\overline G;\\quad\\Lambda=\\nu\\otimes S,\\ \\Lambda_2=\\nu\\Rightarrow\\int Tu\\,d\\nu=\\int u\\,d\\nu.",
          "lean": "Tests.GaussianMarginalPoincare.actual_same_mean_centered_contraction; hSameG; LinearPMap.eq_of_eq_graph; hcompS; hMean; hPreserve; Measure.integral_compProd; integral_map"
        },
        {
          "title": "Consume the exact source C3 and sharp C4 estimate",
          "text": "For centered u the preceding derived domain and centering allow PI on Tu: mη‖Tu‖²≤‖Ku‖². Combine it with actual56 sharp energy η‖Ku‖²≤c(‖u‖²−‖Tu‖²), c=(1−αη)²/[4(1+αη)]. Explicit scalar algebra yields (1+αη)²‖Tu‖²≤(1−αη)²‖u‖². Original α≤β and βη≤1 make ρ=(1−αη)/(1+αη) nonnegative, so squared comparison gives ‖Tu‖≤ρ‖u‖, including αη=1 without dividing by1−αη. Full macro-range, H1 and Γ identity are separate.",
          "formula": "m_\\eta\\|Tu\\|^2\\le\\|Ku\\|^2,\\quad\\eta\\|Ku\\|^2\\le\\frac{(1-\\alpha\\eta)^2}{4(1+\\alpha\\eta)}(\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2)\\Rightarrow\\|Tu\\|\\le\\frac{1-\\alpha\\eta}{1+\\alpha\\eta}\\|u\\|.",
          "lean": "hC3; hSharp; hP; hSharp′; hSq; hSq′; sq_le_sq₀"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, 0<α≤β, α‖a‖²≤D²V(x)[a,a]≤β‖a‖² for every x,a, η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), J=law(X,X+√ηZ) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), and ν=J.snd. Then ν is a probability. There exists one densely defined closable real linear gradient G:L²(ν)⇀L²(ν;E), whose graph consists exactly of AE classes (φ,∇φ) for smooth compactly supported φ, and whose closure has closed graph. For every z in domḠ with ∫z dν=0, [α/(1+αη)]‖z‖²≤‖Ḡz‖². The same G is chosen before every such z. No caller normalization, curvature, Poincare, law, domain, convergence or extra moment certificate is assumed. This is the genuine compact-gradient closure formulation of the source marginal PI; equivalence with a separately defined weighted H1 remains open.",
      "lean_proof": "Derive the actual marginal law and its potential; Produce the true conditional covariance bound; Obtain both exact marginal curvature constants; Apply Poincare on the genuine closed gradient domain; Derive domain agreement and centeredness for the real mean; Consume the exact source C3 and sharp C4 estimate",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GaussianMarginalGradient.gaussian_marginal_gradient_closable",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CenteredDomainPoincare.gibbs_centered_domain_poincare",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsLinearCovarianceUpper.gibbs_linear_covariance_upper",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianConvolutionRegularity.gaussian_convolution_derivatives",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.SmoothedGibbsPotential.smoothed_gibbs_potential",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.SmoothedHessianUpper.smoothed_hessian_upper"
      ],
      "mathlib_dependencies": [
        "Measure.map_map",
        "Measure.tilted_tilted",
        "integral_exp_pos",
        "fderiv_add_const",
        "LinearPMap.eq_of_eq_graph",
        "Measure.disintegrate",
        "Measure.integral_compProd",
        "integral_map",
        "sq_le_sq₀"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
